The plate holds two cross-section pieces of corn on the cob. Each looks about 3 cm long and 4 cm across, so roughly 30-40 g per piece including the cob. The edible kernels are probably 25-30 g per piece, which gives about 70 g total for the food on the plate.

Corn kernels have about 0.9-1.0 kcal/g, so 70 g is roughly 65 kcal.

